course: dictionary
lesson: 6436
title: Mythical: real or imagined?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A myth is an old story, often about gods, heroes or magic creatures. Something mythical comes from those stories, so it is not real. «In 1414 a giraffe from Malindi, in today's Kenya, was brought to the Ming court, where people took it for a qilin, a lucky mythical beast, and painted it.» The words beast and lucky are clues. A qilin is a creature from legends, so mythical means found in stories, not real.
explain: Mythical can also mean imagined or made up, something people believe in but which is not true. Try this check: swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense. «The lucky creature from legends» works, so your meaning is right.
explain: Sometimes people use mythical as a joke. If someone says, «the mythical tidy bedroom», they mean a bedroom that is so tidy it seems never to exist. The context tells you it is a joke, because nobody really thinks such a bedroom is a myth from an old story.
fact: Mythical means found in myths and legends, and not real.
fact: Mythical creatures include dragons, unicorns, the phoenix, mermaids and the kraken.
fact: Mythical can also mean imagined or made up, believed in but not true.
fact: Myths from Greek and Norse stories are often studied in history and religious education.
fact: Mythical is an adjective: more mythical, most mythical.
exercise: «...a qilin, a lucky mythical beast, and painted it.» What does mythical mean here? | *Found in legends, not real | Painted in bright colours | Very large and brown | Lucky, with good luck for everyone
exercise: Which of these is a mythical creature? | A goldfish | A tabby cat | A rabbit | *A unicorn
exercise: Someone jokes, «the mythical tidy bedroom». What does it suggest? | A bedroom that is tidy every day | A bedroom with a new bed | *Something that seems never to exist | A room painted blue
test: Copy one mythical creature from this list: dragon, table, pencil, window. | Window | Pencil | *Dragon | Table
test: Which word is the best swap for mythical in «a mythical beast»? | Tiny | Slow | Real | *Legendary
exam: Dana says a mythical creature is real because she saw one in a book. What is the best answer? | *A mythical creature is not real; it lives in stories | Books show only real things | Dragons are real animals | A book is always true
